window.docContents[123].resolve({"/Abstraction/Parameters-by-reference/#Core-C______--Abstraction--Parameters-by-reference":{"contents":"A parameter  receives the location of its argument, which must denote a location of exactly the type . The binding of  in the function environment is an alias, as in a local reference, and the return does not free it. In  the parameter has the type of its referent.Two reference parameters bound to the same argument alias each other, and a write through one is read through the other, as in C++.\n\n","context":"Core C++\u0009Abstraction","header":"5.2. Parameters by reference","id":"/Abstraction/Parameters-by-reference/#Core-C______--Abstraction--Parameters-by-reference"}});